# A local may shadow a unit-level constant of another unit -- `arch` is also
# `platform.arch`, an `archkind` value. The base of a dotted read is asked by
# its SOURCE name and only when no local answers to it, so `arch.stringView`
# reads the local under either naming scheme (`--readable-names` makes the
# local's C identifier its source name, which is what made the two diverge).
main: function is {
    arch: "/nonexistent-shadow-case".string
    hit: io.exists path: arch.stringView
    if hit then print "exists" else print "missing"
    print "arch: \{arch}"
}
